<title>USA: Apollon starts herpes vaccine trial.</title>
<headline>Apollon starts herpes vaccine trial.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apollon Inc said on Wednesday it had started a Phase I clinical trial of a DNA-based genetic vaccine targeting the herpes simplex virus.</p>
<p>The vaccine is being developed with American Home Products Corp's Wyeth-Lederle Vaccines and Pediatrics unit.</p>
<p>The main objective of the Phase I trial is to establish the safety of the vaccine and evaluate immune responses it stimulates.  Forty healthy people will be enrolled.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
</text>
